# adversarial-review capability — promotion into canonical loam — apply ladder

Per `docs/plans/release-integration-v1-10-0-adversarial-review.md` (a
LIFT of the pos3 build-plan + determinations, not a fresh derivation).
loam's standing adversarial-review capability lands as a NEW opt-in
component `framework/adversarial-review/` (0.1.0, out-of-graph +
out-of-lockstep this cut, D-AR-LOCK) plus the discoverable
`adversarial-review` SKILL added to the sealed loam-skills plugin.

The capability defeats the ways AI review goes soft (sycophancy,
agreement bias, self-preference, generic critique, hallucinated flaws,
panel consensus-collapse, performed harshness) STRUCTURALLY — by how
the review is constructed — never by asking a model to be brutal.

  - AC.AR.1 (outcome-altitude) — the manual on-demand entry
    (`manual.review_file`) points at ONE artifact + its stated
    objective and returns a structured harsh review: findings each
    pinned to location + concrete failure scenario + severity, plus a
    verdict. No gate, no block. The real entry fn runs over a real
    file with no pre-arranged state.
  - AC.AR.2 — the critic seed (`seed.py`) is artifact + objective +
    methodology + protocol ONLY; the parent conversation, the author's
    self-assessment, owner enthusiasm, and authorship provenance are
    excluded (sycophancy is preference-trained and rides the polluted
    parent context — the isolation is the counter).
  - AC.AR.3 — the derive phase seed EXCLUDES the artifact bytes; the
    diff phase carries the derivation + the artifact. The two-spawn
    ordering is structural, so the "what a correct artifact must
    contain" derivation is authentically artifact-blind (Nemeth: a
    position the critic constructed itself is genuinely held).
  - AC.AR.4 — a finding blocks only AFTER a ground-truth validation
    pass (`validation.py`) re-checks it; unvalidated findings
    quarantine as HYPOTHESIZED — visible, severity-capped, never
    blocking. Keeps critic recall HIGH and spends precision in
    validation, never by making the critic timid.
  - AC.AR.5 — the gate verdict (`verdict.py`) BLOCKs by default on
    validated top-severity findings; the owner override is an explicit,
    recorded act; a PASS that fails to name (a) its strongest surviving
    objection and (b) what the review could not check is malformed and
    rejected.
  - AC.AR.6 — zero validated substantive findings on a nontrivial
    artifact raises a suspicion flag on the REVIEW itself, not a clean
    bill (a shallow review that looks harsh is anti-evidence — F7).
  - AC.AR.7 — a finding that would be true of any artifact of the class
    ("could be more robust") is flagged generic and excluded from the
    verdict calculus (generic critique is the failure that most
    resembles success — Liang).
  - AC.AR.8 — every critic / merge-judge / non-executable validator
    spawn routes through the SEALED `spawn_isolated_claude`
    (`spawn.py`); a hand-rolled bare `claude` argv (missing
    `--strict-mcp-config`/`--mcp-config`) is refused — the un-isolated
    spawn is the proven Telegram-death kill vector, not a style
    preference. The sealed surface is imported, never edited (Lens 1).
  - AC.AR.9 — the domain-methodology corpus (`corpus.py`) is checked
    BEFORE any research pull; a kept doc is indexed with its citations
    and reused by a later same-domain review; the two seed docs
    (domain-agnostic layer) ship present. Review N+1 is cheaper +
    sharper than review N — the standing capability's memory.
  - AC.AR.10 (outcome-altitude) — feeding a seeded-flaw artifact
    (`calibration.py`) reads back a computed catch rate; the harness
    matches critic findings to the seeded flaws. A reviewer whose
    detection rate is never measured is faith, not protection — the
    real calibration proof (`calibration/CALIBRATION-RESULT.md`, catch
    1.0 on the seeded proof) is the recall evidence.
  - AC.AR.11 — the STANDARD floor (one two-phase falsification critic +
    validation + verdict) is non-skippable for a boundary artifact;
    DEEP (`tiers.py`) adds parallel per-axis isolated critics with NO
    shared context + a separate merge judge preserving disagreement.
    A symmetric free-form panel is never the mechanism (unguided panels
    collapse into consensus).
  - AC.AR.12 — the auto-blocking boundary gate (`gate.py`) is a no-op
    while the activation switch is OFF (the default). It ships
    EXPERIMENTAL: it is NOT the named v1.10.0 outcome, and it may not
    be activated to auto-block any real boundary until a measured
    false-positive / precision test on clean artifacts is recorded
    (recall is proven; precision is not — a gate that blocks good work
    is worse than no gate). Activation is a separate owner-gated
    amendment. The manual entry works regardless of the switch.
  - AC.AR.13 — review output carries NO stakeholder-reaction-prediction
    framing (`critic.py`); a lint rejects "they will think / how X will
    receive it" — the critic answers "can this survive attack?", never
    "how will X receive it?" (a generic skeptical-adversary model
    applied to a bought-in counterparty misjudges the human).

